          %p Uniqueness rules for the interval type:
          %p …
          %h2#properties Properties
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                An interval type is provably
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contractible+type"} contractible
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/typal+equality"} typal equality
            %li
              %p
                An interval type is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/suspension+type"} suspension type
                of the
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+type"} unit type
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/globe"} globe
                type.
            %li
              %p
                An interval type is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cone+type"} cone type
                of the unit type.
            %li
              %p
                An interval type is a
                %span.newWikiWord
                  cubical type
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/cubical+type"} ?
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mo □
                          %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Box^1
          %h3#induction_principle_without_heterogeneous_identifications Induction principle without heterogeneous identifications
          %p
            There is a version of the induction principle which uses a type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            and a function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi 𝕀
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:C \to \mathbb{I}
            instead of a type family
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
